387
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:10,550
Note after the ending.

388
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:34,720
Wang Ping's story to the throne was heavily expanded upon in the donghua. Some notable changes from the novel include the fact Wang Ping didn't rise from rebuilding a village but he instead created a mortal sect called the School of Heaven. His sect grew in power until it rivaled the other countries and conquered them.

When Wang Ping goes back to his hometown, he meets Zhou Ruotong, his childhood love, with her daughter. When they start walking with Qing Yi towards Sun Tai's grave, the little girl says her name. 

Wang Ping asked, “Is this your daughter?”
The woman nodded. She turned toward the girl and said, “Call him ‘uncle’. He was your mother’s childhood friend.”
The girl seemed a bit shy. She stood behind her mother and whispered, “Uncle…”
Just after Wang Ping walked several steps, the little girl hiding behind her mother exposed her head and shouted, “Uncle, my name is Xu Nianping!”
Xu being her family name, and Nianping meaning "remember Ping".

Later, when Wang Ping goes back to his father, he doesn't ask about his origins but about his mother specifically.
“Dad, I want to know about my mother…”
It had been more than 60 years since Wang Ping first asked this. He remembered that he had only asked this once, and he saw how crestfallen his father was that time. This was the second time he asked.

After that, when they lived in that small mountain village, we learn that Qing Yi has reached Soul Formation on her own after Wang Lin raised her to Nascent Soul. Her domain is regretless passion. Qing Yi aged herself artificially like Wang Lin.

